//@version=6

// ============================================================================
// TP_Ephem_Lib — Cowan-tailored heliocentric ephemeris for TradingView Pine v6
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Theory:    VSOP87D (Bretagnon & Francou 1988), heliocentric ecliptic of date.
// Source:    IMCCE FTP (https://ftp.imcce.fr/pub/ephem/planets/vsop87/)
// Coverage:  Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune
// Frame:     Heliocentric ecliptic of date (matches Cowan canon V4:L239).
//            Sidereal correction is applied via the `useSidereal` flag.
// Accuracy:  Truncated to top-N terms by amplitude per L_p sub-series.
//            Inner planets (Mer/Ven/Ear/Mar): L0=80 L1=50 L2=30 L3=15 L4=8 L5=4
//            Outer planets (Jup/Sat/Ura/Nep): L0=50 L1=25 L2=15 L3=8  L4=4 L5=2
//            Expected accuracy at this truncation:
//              Mer 0.01-0.05 deg | Ven/Ear ~0.005 deg | Mar 0.005-0.02 deg
//              Jup/Sat/Ura/Nep ~0.001-0.01 deg
//            Well within Cowan day-precision needs (V1:L2080 1% tolerance).
// Date range: 1850-2100 nominal; degrades gracefully outside.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Cowan-specific helpers (added in subsequent build steps):
//   - cumulative_advance_deg     — V4:L5079 (3-Step Astro)
//   - synodic_phase              — direct angular separation between two planets
//   - synodic_harmonic_crossings — dates where synodic crosses 15/22.5/30/45/60/90 deg
//   - pentagram_vertex_dates     — Uranus 72 deg vertices (V4 pentagonal cycles)
//   - cube_face_boundary_dates   — V1 cube faces (S-U 90/180/270/360/540 + Uranus 360)
//   - is_retrograde / speed_deg_per_day
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// MIT License
